    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (32 tests, 0 failures/errors), including the new `Cp21Tests` audit test.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** (new function class) \u2014 reads the persisted `@Val Owner` and emits an INFO line on the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` containing the owner id, customerCode and registrationDate:\n   ```\n   INFO  AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-11\n   ```\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `audit` step in the pipeline between `save` and `respond`. It runs *after* `save` so the DB-generated owner id is available, and shares `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\n**Why it's placed after save:** the id is only assigned once the owner is persisted, and `@Val Owner` yields the same in-place object, so the audit step sees the assigned id plus the already-set customerCode and registrationDate. The registrationDate is logged via `LocalDate.toString()`, which produces the same ISO-8601 text (`2026-08-11`) the response DTO serializes \u2014 matching how the test compares against `o.get(\"registrationDate\").asText()`.\n\nAll 32 tests pass, including the new `Cp21Tests.coreLogsAuditOnCreate`.",
